From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: haroldxie <xiewenhao2308@icloud.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 10:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: fpsimd: export fpsimd_load_state() and
 fpsimd_save_state() for the KJIT runtime

The KJIT runtime runs verified translations of a task's user code at EL1
on the syscall return path, before the task goes back to userspace. Some
of that code (glibc memcpy, memset, strlen) uses FP/SIMD registers, and
the translation keeps V0-V31, FPCR and FPSR as the user's registers.

The runtime runs such code in a preemptible task-level kernel-mode NEON
section. kernel_neon_begin(&buf) saves the user state to thread.uw and
takes the registers, the context switch path then saves and restores the
registers in buf (TIF_KERNEL_FPSTATE) on any CPU, and the runtime copies
the user state in and out with the raw helpers:

	kernel_neon_begin(&buf);
	fpsimd_load_state(&current->thread.uw.fpsimd_state);
	/* run the translated user code, preemptible */
	fpsimd_save_state(&current->thread.uw.fpsimd_state);
	current->thread.fpsimd_cpu = NR_CPUS;
	kernel_neon_end(&buf);

The return to userspace then reloads the updated state (the section
leaves TIF_FOREIGN_FPSTATE set). Both helpers are plain register <->
memory copies in entry-fpsimd.S and need none of the surrounding
bookkeeping, so export them GPL-only. Nothing else changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/kernel/fpsimd.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/kernel/fpsimd.c b/arch/arm64/kernel/fpsimd.c
--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/fpsimd.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/fpsimd.c
@@ -1983,6 +1983,14 @@
 	}
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(kernel_neon_end);
+
+/*
+ * Raw copies between memory and V0-V31, FPSR and FPCR, for a task-level
+ * kernel_neon_begin() section that runs on a given user_fpsimd_state. Only
+ * valid between kernel_neon_begin() and kernel_neon_end().
+ */
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(fpsimd_load_state);
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(fpsimd_save_state);
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_EFI
 
